{"Device-limit enforcement is non-atomic: CountDevices(...) is executed and then INSERT ... ON CONFLICT is performed, allowing concurrent requests to observe count < limit and insert/update concurrently, temporarily exceeding the configured limit": 0.8912173509597778, "ErrDeviceLimitReached is a plain error, so when it bubbles up through auth middleware it gets turned into a generic 401 Unauthorized response, losing the real reason. It should be an errutil error (e.g., 429) with a public message so API clients can distinguish it": 0.935880720615387, "device_limit is read from [auth.anonymous] but is not present in conf/defaults.ini's [auth.anonymous] section, making the new setting undiscoverable for users and won't appear in the default config shipped with Grafana": 0.8123892545700073, "Device-limit enforcement adds an extra COUNT query to every tagged request when the limit is enabled": 0.6219802498817444, "The new test only asserts that inserting a new device fails once the limit is reached, but doesn't verify that an existing device can still be updated when the limit is reached (the updateDevice path)": 0.7274620532989502}